SQLite terminology databases used by Convert-Pheno.

The databases are organized as a versioned bundle:

```
share/db/
  README
  manifest.json
  concepts_candidates_2_exposure.csv
  v0/
    cdisc.db
    hpo.db
    icd10.db
    ncit.db
    ohdsi.db
    omim.db
```

`manifest.json` lists the database versions, row counts, checksums, and active
bundle. Its `currentBundle` field currently points to `v0`. Using this file
instead of a symbolic link works consistently on Unix and Windows.

The smaller databases are included with Convert-Pheno. Because `ohdsi.db` is
approximately 3.2 GB, it is downloaded separately. Place it in the active
bundle directory (`share/db/v0/`), or keep it elsewhere and provide its
directory with `--path-to-ohdsi-db`. Do not place it directly in `share/db/`.

## Terminology sources and terms for bundle v0

Convert-Pheno is distributed under the Artistic License 2.0. The terminology
content indexed by these SQLite databases comes from third-party resources and
remains subject to the terms and attribution requirements of each source. The
SQLite files contain selected identifiers and labels arranged for local search;
they do not replace the corresponding source terminology.

| Database | Content snapshot | Source/download | License or terms |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `ncit.db` | NCI Thesaurus 22.06d | [NCIt on BioPortal](https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/NCIT) | [NCI Thesaurus Terms of Use](https://evs.nci.nih.gov/ftp1/NCI_Thesaurus/ThesaurusTermsofUse.htm) (CC BY 4.0) |
| `icd10.db` | CDC ICD-10-CM 2026, released 2025-06-12 | [CDC ICD-10-CM files](https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/icd/icd-10-cm/files.html) | [CDC use of agency materials](https://www.cdc.gov/other/agencymaterials.html) |
| `cdisc.db` | CDISC SDTM Controlled Terminology, downloaded 2023-01-24 | [NCI EVS SDTM Terminology](https://evs.nci.nih.gov/ftp1/CDISC/SDTM/) | [CDISC Controlled Terminology](https://www.cdisc.org/standards/terminology/controlled-terminology) |
| `omim.db` | OMIM phenotype table, downloaded 2023-05-22 | [macarthur-lab OMIM data](https://github.com/macarthur-lab/omim) | [OMIM use agreement](https://www.omim.org/help/agreement) |
| `hpo.db` | Human Phenotype Ontology v2023-04-05 | [HPO v2023-04-05](https://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/hp/releases/2023-04-05/hp.obo) | [HPO license and citation information](https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology/blob/master/LICENSE.md) |
| `ohdsi.db` | OHDSI Standardized Vocabularies v5.0, 29-AUG-22 | [Athena](https://athena.ohdsi.org/) | [Athena vocabulary access and licensing](https://ohdsi.github.io/BookOfOhdsi-2ndEdition/representation/vocabularies.html) |

For current terms or redistribution, consult the upstream links. Please cite
the original terminology resources in scientific work where they are used.

## OHDSI database contents

The release was obtained from the vocabulary_version entry in VOCABULARY.csv.
The current database is approximately 3.2 GB. In addition to concept labels and
identifiers, it contains OMOP domain and standard-concept metadata plus active
`Maps to` and `Maps to value` relationships. These fields are required for
domain-aware standard concept resolution when OMOP is the output model.
